    You decide to move toward the north.
 
The barbarian attacks you with 180 units of power!
But you survive the attack!
No one leaves the dungeon without the Power Ring!
 
    You decide to move toward the south.
 
The barbarian attacks you with 170 units of power!
But you survive the attack!
As you move into the next room,
you see that you are in a damp, dark cave.
 
To the north is a stairway going up.
To the south is a passage way.
To the east is a steel door.
To the west is a granite wall.
 
At your feet you see the Dungeon Keeper's keys.
Your psychic powers sense the Power Ring toward the east.
 
    You decide to move toward the east.
You force the door open,
but it took 500 units of power.
After you pass through the door,
an Orc runs up and slams it shut behind you.
 
You discover that you are in a cavern full of bats.
 
To the north is a passage way.
To the south is a passage way.
To the east is a stone wall with a map on it.
To the west is a steel door.
 
At your feet you see a pile of golden nuggets.
In front of you is a crafty old alchemist, smiling.
Your psychic powers sense the Power Ring toward the east.
 
    You decide to look around.
 
You are in a cavern full of bats.
 
To the north is a passage way.
To the south is a passage way.
To the east is a stone wall with a map on it.
To the west is a steel door.
 
At your feet you see a pile of golden nuggets.
In front of you is a crafty old alchemist, smiling.
Your psychic powers sense the Power Ring toward the east.
 
 
    You decide to take the pile of golden nuggets.
But it is only fool's gold, which you throw away in disgust!
 
 
    You decide to move toward the west.
 
The crafty old alchemist attacks you with 18180 units of power!
 
 
Oh, dear!
 
I'm afraid that my little pets would have
killed you had I not arrived at the last moment!
You really must be more careful!
 
But then you can't win them all, you know,
and this next dungeon of mine is so easy,
you can't lose!
Would you like to play again? No way!
Well, please come again.
 
